WEBVTT

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:02.430
I wonder where Kiyoko went?

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:13.850
It's just a series of troubles for her brother.

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:15.280
I guess he can't bear to sit still.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:17.840
Isamu hasn't come back either.

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:21.390
He said he was going to search for her, but I'll bet he's off fooling around somewhere...

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:23.350
...because he doesn't want to shovel snow.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:30.910
Kiyoko!

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:03.410
Tatsuya, you still can't control your power.

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:07.620
One clumsy slip and you would've killed not just them but Kiyoko too.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.580
I forget, can you teleport?

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:30.920
No...

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:34.050
Even if they locked her up, it's still inside this hotel.

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:35.610
It's not a major problem.

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:40.550
I'll let you see her.

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:41.960
Okay...

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:44.030
Toru...

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:53.840
Here it comes, okay?

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:01.240
A nosebleed again!

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.140
Just kidding!

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:08.480
Well, shall we go?

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:10.250
What should I do?

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:14.320
You keep a close watch, over the Countess.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:20.460
So it's true: "Always set a thief to catch a thief."

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:25.600
If I may say so, we may not look it, but we're upstanding brokers.

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:29.430
So you say the place you found her was quite nearby?

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:34.180
You know how they say it's darkest at the base of the lighthouse.

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:36.740
What was she doing there?

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:45.580
She was talking to a rabbit made from snow?

00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:48.860
Yes...

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:52.130
About what?

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:54.020
That much we didn't hear.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.370
Are you okay?

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:38.810
Just a little worn out. I did get away.

00:06:39.680 --> 00:06:41.910
Although I ended up in this situation.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:48.110
Why did you go by yourself? We've always been together.

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:53.690
If I had said something, would you have come with me?

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:00.260
You said it yourself, Tatsuya.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:03.570
You said you're going to stay here and face Dad.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:06.130
But I don't want to.

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:12.540
Now was the perfect time for us to start walking separate paths.

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:16.810
I don't want anything like that! We'll always stay together, right?

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:21.480
You're not a child anymore either. You can make it on your own, right?

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:25.120
Let's go, let's escape from here together.

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:37.030
I'm very sorry, but I can't let you do that.

00:07:42.910 --> 00:07:45.930
Fu, you're here, aren't you?

00:07:46.950 --> 00:07:48.150
Toru...

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:49.350
I'm sorry.

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:52.780
There's nothing to apologize for. You're a good boy, Toru.

00:07:53.150 --> 00:07:56.350
You don't understand if doing this sort of thing is right or wrong?

00:07:56.350 --> 00:08:01.020
Not exactly, I just didn't think this was any way to treat Kiyoko.

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:03.690
Let's talk about that later.

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:06.890
I'm guessing you haven't finished shoveling yet.

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:10.590
You're going to disobey me?

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:13.430
Do you want to be treated as you once were?

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:17.170
Take Tatsuya with you, and go immediately.

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:19.500
I'm not going.

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:25.850
There are things I want to speak to Kiyoko about privately.

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:27.450
But...

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:32.390
Go, Tatsuya. I have things to say to that woman too.

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:50.200
Fu, weren't you listening?

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:53.340
Let's go.

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:06.180
You always do that: try to control people by intimidation.

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:11.530
For a girl who hasn't gone to school, you know some big words.

00:09:14.800 --> 00:09:16.460
Intimidation...

00:09:18.170 --> 00:09:21.400
You look horrid, just like a drowned rat.

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:25.100
I don't know why you thought you'd run away,

00:09:25.610 --> 00:09:29.270
...when you could live here and lack for nothing.

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:33.950
Or will you parrot Gilgamesh?

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:36.420
What's here is only meaningless junk?

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:42.020
Whatever you may say, you were loitering near the hotel,

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:44.690
...so you wanted to be caught, didn't you?

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.690
Because you were worried about your brother?

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:50.000
That's part of it.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:52.030
Such charming love between siblings.

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:55.640
You thought he might be maltreated out of spite?

00:09:56.470 --> 00:09:58.440
By the scary lady?

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:02.150
No, not that, just the opposite.

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:03.670
The opposite?

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:11.580
I was very worried that you might do something to Tatsuya.

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:15.150
And what is that something?

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:17.750
Something I can't say out loud.

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:22.660
It's because when you looked at him,

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:26.700
...your eyes looked, how can I say it, deviant.

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:33.240
I thought I'd give you a warning, as his sister, so nothing like that happens.

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:53.860
I only wanted to say that.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.970
What a shameless thing to say!

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:24.750
What's going to happen to my sister?

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:27.490
I don't know that either.

00:11:28.670 --> 00:11:32.300
The Countess is talking to her attorneys right now.

00:11:32.300 --> 00:11:33.740
Attorneys?

00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:35.370
The fact is...

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:39.780
These past two or three days, I was at the place where you two grew up.

00:11:39.780 --> 00:11:42.780
I thought it might give us a hint in looking for Kiyoko.

00:11:42.780 --> 00:11:44.150
You saw it?

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:45.410
Yeah...

00:11:46.320 --> 00:11:49.950
Maybe I shouldn't say it, but it's amazing you turned out so well.

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:53.180
It's because Kiyoko was there for me.

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:40.100
Kiyoko...

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:19.810
Here it comes!

00:13:22.310 --> 00:13:23.940
Tatsuya!

00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:24.260
That stupid Tatsuya!

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:26.330
We'll always stay together!

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:29.080
Bonehead!

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:32.180
We won't be lonely or anything.

00:14:33.080 --> 00:14:35.110
We won't be lonely or anything, you know.

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:37.080
We won't be lonely...

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:22.300
Did you think maybe your sister was playing?

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:24.660
A little...

00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:28.530
I can't play as well as her.

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:38.210
I woke you, didn't I? I'm sorry.

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:40.720
No...

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:43.480
Kiyoko will be leaving here tomorrow.

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:46.760
It's something we mutually agreed on.

00:15:46.760 --> 00:15:50.520
I can't allow her to remain here.

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:53.220
You'll be staying here.

00:15:55.030 --> 00:15:59.030
I'm having the papers regarding this case made up now.

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:04.400
Kiyoko will pay back the money little by little as she works.

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:10.710
She was saying some dreamlike things about becoming a piano tuner.

00:16:11.520 --> 00:16:14.890
But that's because that was really Kiyoko's dream.

00:16:14.890 --> 00:16:18.620
Ah, how good to be young, and to be able to believe in your dreams.

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:21.780
But reality is not so kind, you know.

00:16:22.630 --> 00:16:26.790
Well, would you let me see her?

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:32.430
No, not now. Not until all the procedures are finished.

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:37.700
I'm not saying that to be mean. Don't think ill of me.

00:16:42.650 --> 00:16:44.320
Would you like a drink?

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:45.580
No thank you.

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:48.880
You don't like drunk women?

00:16:50.250 --> 00:16:51.650
To tell the truth...

00:16:52.660 --> 00:16:56.290
You're a good boy, aren't you? Show me your face a little better.

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:26.090
Forget about this...

00:17:26.660 --> 00:17:27.890
I know.

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:32.230
Goodnight. You go to bed now too.

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:55.910
I've brought Miss Kiyoko.

00:17:56.820 --> 00:17:58.290
I'm coming.

00:18:02.690 --> 00:18:04.250
Just a brief moment, please.

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:11.090
I hate getting older.

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:13.800
I can't appear in front of people without transforming myself.

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:15.970
Like a ghost trying to appear in the daylight.

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:26.380
A copy of the agreement you checked yesterday. You hold on to this.

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:31.320
I don't know how much the tuning business will pay,

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:34.620
...but your whole life will be spent just paying the interest.

00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:36.690
You have no regrets about this?

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:38.890
No...

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:41.700
You can't run away or hide, you know.

00:18:42.570 --> 00:18:44.030
I know.

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:50.840
As for Gilgamesh, even if something happens like before,

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:52.930
...I won't do anything to help.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:56.910
I will abandon you, so that's what you should expect.

00:18:57.010 --> 00:19:00.470
They said they won't do anything like that again.

00:19:00.650 --> 00:19:04.710
Quite understanding, aren't they? One more thing...

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:08.380
Gilgamesh aren't human.

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:12.990
It's time.

00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:18.120
Kiyoko!

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:27.640
I don't know what to say. If I had been a little stronger person...

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:30.440
No, it's not your fault.

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:32.580
I'll write you a letter, okay?

00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:34.780
Teach me piano next time too!

00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:36.310
Sure...

00:19:39.520 --> 00:19:43.550
We thank you for your patronage of the Hotel Providence.

00:19:44.060 --> 00:19:46.790
We eagerly await your next visit.

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:48.850
Thank you for everything.

00:19:50.970 --> 00:19:53.070
Hey, where's Tatsuya?

00:19:53.070 --> 00:19:54.630
He's feeling bashful.

00:20:18.430 --> 00:20:20.760
You jerk, now I'm all wet.

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:27.440
You're going?

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:28.910
Yeah...

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:31.970
Here's something important to you.

00:20:35.010 --> 00:20:36.380
Thanks.

00:20:37.280 --> 00:20:40.150
Kiyoko, I...

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:46.390
See you.

00:20:46.390 --> 00:20:47.720
Yeah...

00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:26.150
Turangalila?

00:23:26.150 --> 00:23:30.450
I never even thought that there might be people seriously trying to get rid of that sky.

00:23:30.450 --> 00:23:32.960
...it was somehow like a different world.

00:23:32.960 --> 00:23:33.820
But it is amazing.

00:23:33.820 --> 00:23:34.760
How can I say it?

00:23:34.760 --> 00:23:36.190
I felt like the power of humanity isn't totally lost.

00:23:36.190 --> 00:23:37.990
Your face looks like a criminal's?

00:23:38.300 --> 00:23:39.860
...because until now I only knew what life was like in a local town.

00:23:39.860 --> 00:23:41.770
Before, I spent my life just running away,

00:23:41.770 --> 00:23:43.830
...but I wondered a little if that was good enough?

00:23:43.830 --> 00:23:46.370
The same with living at the Hotel Providence.

00:23:46.370 --> 00:23:47.640
I felt like, "So there's this world too."

00:23:47.640 --> 00:23:49.870
And now there are these people building that kind of tower.

00:23:49.870 --> 00:23:53.430
I wonder how that Enuma lady and the Countess know each other?
